## 5. Evidence gaps flagged for the swarm

- Current MWAA Design Manual sections on acoustics, PA zoning, and EVACS could not be retrieved in this pass. Confirm whether an existing STI or reverberation criterion is already in the manual before the standard is drafted, so a "new" standard is not silently regressive.
- Current TSA guidance on required security announcement cadence, wording, and multilingual coverage was not verified in this pass. Quiet-by-design cannot override a TSA security directive; the operative TSA guidance should be pulled before requirements are written.
- The precise PSAP arrangement at IAD and DCA — whether MWAA dispatch is a primary PSAP for a defined terminal geofence or whether wireless 911 calls default to Loudoun/Arlington — was not directly verified and is the highest-value fact for the standard to pin down.
- A public MWAA after-action report from a major active-assailant exercise or real incident since 2020 was not located in this pass. If one exists internally, its lessons should be integrated before the standard is finalized.
